  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: a698bb9d818e5eb46b964f00c0a9be53, type: 3}
  m_Name: LoreMessages
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  loreMessages:
  - Level: 0
    Message: 'Maintenance report #52


      The AC unit on the roof should be replaced.
      I managed to patch it up for now, but it won''t hold up for long. If I get
      called here one more time management can suffocate for all I care.


      -
      J.G.

'
  - Level: 1
    Message: "Fwd: Project funds\n\LThe boys at purchasing are wondering if we\u2019re
      cleared for that additional funding for Project Molar? They want to get the
      orders sorted by Friday, so please confirm the status of allocated funds with
      Richardson at your earliest convenience.\n\L- Lester"
  - Level: 1
    Message: "Re: Re: Costs\_\n\LCFO wants to know about the procurement costs of
      the Material.\nCould you send the relevant sheets to statistics? Also, let\u2019s
      have\nlegal prepped and ready for any potential leaks.\n\L- Paterson"
  - Level: 1
    Message: "Strategy pivot\n\LIt\u2019s official, the board has officially greenlit
      the proposal. It\u2019s enough to keep our heads above water, but let\u2019s
      make sure the team is on the same page so that we focus on mission-critical
      stuff only. Keep the red tape to a minimum, but make sure they continue to
      understand how far up the good old NDA boot is in their ass, got it?\n\L- Voss"
  - Level: 2
    Message: "Maintenance report #46\L\LWhen prospecting for reno, there was evidence
      of some parts of the wall being hollow on each floor. No sign of this in the
      blueprints, but should be confirmed before the construction starts.\n\L- J.G."
  - Level: 2
    Message: "Re: Leads on Buyers\n\LWe\u2019ve got a tip from John in Accounting
      that the folks at EngiCo had heard some good stuff about the new product. Might
      be worth setting up a meeting. Check in with Hobb on how you\u2019d like to
      proceed.\n\L- Colt"
  - Level: 2
    Message: "Auditory Concerns\n\LI have recent feedback from our receptionists.
      The disruptions have, unfortunately, become increasingly frequent. HQ visitors
      are taking notice, which should cause concern. Can you make sure your guys
      are on this so that we get the structural concerns taken care of? It\u2019s
      not great for optics and frankly, beyond urgent. Make sure to give me an ETA
      when you have one.\n\L- B.L."
  - Level: 2
    Message: "Your cut\n\LI stashed your cut in the toilet. I admit it's hella nasty
      but at least we can be sure nobody's gonna be snooping around in there.\n\L-
      J"
  - Level: 3
    Message: "Comms on M\n\LWe got word that the press has got hold of some documents
      about the specs of Project Molar. Let\u2019s get the Comms on this and workshop
      on our angle in sufficiently tackling this. We don\u2019t want any more bloodhounds
      in the HQ trying to sniff things out. Set up a meeting ASAP and make sure the
      C-level is clued in. It\u2019s clear some housekeeping is due.\n\L- Voss"
  - Level: 3
    Message: "Maintenance report #25\L\LWe need to get see if something can be done
      to the garage. There are three massive halls and only a handful of parking
      spaces. And half the time they are blocking air vents!\n\L- J.G."
  - Level: 3
    Message: "Maintenance report #37\n\LSome suits reported that their vehicles had
      been damaged on the north-east side of the garage. We need someone to review
      the footage from the security camera. Let me know if you find anything. \L-
      J.G."
  - Level: 3
    Message: "Re: Q4 Financials\n\LThanks Rob. I glanced at the numbers and wanted
      to confirm if the security spending is accurately reported. Have we double-checked
      this with the department head? It also seems the security personnel are constantly
      changing on a drop of a hat. Is the churn truly that bad? We should properly
      drill down on this to plug this drain on our HQ ops.\n\n- J.P."
  - Level: 3
    Message: "Hot Goss\n\LYoo I just saw a guy armed to the teeth enter the classified
      area. I mean.. what the hell is even going on there? Also, not seen the OG
      security guys around for a while now. Missing my eye candy, Derek! I wonder
      what happened to him, huh?\n\L- Leah"
  - Level: 4
    Message: "Maintenance report #43\n\LThere's been reports on rodents spotted in
      the premises, especially on the lower levels. We need an estimate on structural
      integrity and see if we need to get the pest control on this.\n\L- J.G."
  - Level: 4
    Message: "Re: Layout\n\LThanks for the update! I wanted to inquire if the draft
      issue I mentioned is going to be addressed as part of this reno? It\u2019s
      been a problem for a while, but recently, there\u2019s also been this unpleasant
      smell coming from the side of the drafty wall. I would strongly recommend checking
      it out and getting it sorted, so that we can focus on our job in a better environment.\n\L-
      Sue"
  - Level: 4
    Message: "Maintenance report #6\L\LThe new security gate marks the start of the
      classified area. We've been requested not to enter under any circumstances
      and the area does not fall under our responsibility. Just keep out of there.\n\L-
      J.G."
  - Level: 4
    Message: "Re: Regarding the incident\n\LThe parties involved have been sent for
      a psych eval, and we\u2019ll continue their rehabilitation from there. No reason
      to worry. We are confident in their full recovery.\n\L- Voss"
  - Level: 4
    Message: "To B,\n\LI believe it is in our great interest to further our efforts
      in our mutually beneficial transaction. Let\u2019s meet in the usual spot.
      I\u2019m sure the agenda is clear. I\u2019ll be waiting.\n\L- C"
  - Level: 4
    Message: "Have you noticed Cal and Bo sneaking off lately? I\u2019m starting
      to think they\u2019ve been selected for that project people are whispering
      about. I can\u2019t believe every opportunity in this company just flies straight
      over my head. Maybe we should ask one of them to join us for lunch to get some
      hints on what they\u2019ve been up to, what do you think?\n\n- Rey"
